YOLOv8s vs YOLOv8n ablation | TEST | deterministic val (rect=True, batch=1)
========================================================================
  model | params(M) |  GFLOPs | mAP@0.5 | mAP@.5:.95
------------------------------------------------------------
  n@320 |      3.01 |    2.02 |   0.334 |      0.192
  n@640 |      3.01 |    8.09 |   0.594 |      0.373
  s@320 |     11.13 |    7.11 |   0.485 |      0.281
  s@640 |     11.13 |   28.45 |   0.719 |      0.478

n vs s at matched input size:
  @320: ΔmAP@0.5 = +0.152  ΔmAP@.5:.95 = +0.089  | s costs 3.5× GFLOPs (11.1M vs 3.0M params)
        device est: n 12 FPS -> s ≈ 3.4 FPS (cost model: latency ∝ GFLOPs)
  @640: ΔmAP@0.5 = +0.124  ΔmAP@.5:.95 = +0.105  | s costs 3.5× GFLOPs (11.1M vs 3.0M params)
        device est: n 4 FPS -> s ≈ 1.1 FPS (cost model: latency ∝ GFLOPs)

Verdict: YOLOv8s buys the accuracy deltas above for ~3-4× the compute (=> ~1/3 the device FPS).
For a real-time mobile target, YOLOv8n is the justified choice unless the accuracy gain is essential.